{"base_rate":0.17584097859327216,"brier":0.10480550458715596,"bss":0.2768090473501654,"bss_hi":0.38132787714146266,"bss_lo":0.17645199996747754,"chart":{"base":[290.0,62.3],"fp":[263.6,364.9],"lead":"62,280.7 272,265.5 482,242.1 692,201.3","note":{"base":"skill 0.28 — higher than 46% of cities","fp":"low end +6pp, high end +1pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.8 °C — better than 92% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 6%; promised 49% → rained 54%"},"rel":"62,441.1 98.5,407.5 371.5,230.7"},"country":"TN","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.062477064220183495,"ess":315.83465915326707,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Sfax</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Sfax rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (70%), believe about\n<b>70%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>6%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 654 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 4.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.28, ranked 115 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(62&ndash;154) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>365</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'><b>15%</b></td><td class='num'>84</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>26%</td><td class='num'><b>38%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>70%</td><td class='num'><b>70%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Sfax</b> <span class=\"muted\">Tunisia</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.28</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>62&ndash;154\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>654 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Sfax &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Sfax\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" 